inline_comments.body:
This puts a DeepEP-specific branch into the shared `RoutedExperts.forward` (`isinstance(self.token_dispatcher, DeepEPTokenDispatcher)`), and decides it on every forward through duck typing (`getattr(metadata, "routed_scores_R", None)`, `getattr(self.w2, "bias", None)`). `GroupedLinear` always has a `bias` attribute, so the second `getattr` can just be `self.w2.bias`.

The fallback branch (`output_postprocess` or a w2 bias, which means muse_spark or gpt_oss) has no in-repo DeepEP consumer: the only DeepEP recipes are qwen3 MoE (`torchtitan_recipes/tests/models/qwen3.py`, `rl/search_r1.py`, `tests/rl/alphabet_sort.py`). The smallest version of this PR:
- reject DeepEP + `output_postprocess`/w2 bias with a `ValueError` in `RoutedExperts.Config.__post_init__`;
- always absorb `metadata.routed_scores_R` when the metadata is `DeepEPDispatchMetadata`;
- drop the `combine_kwargs` plumbing, the `routed_scores_R` kwarg on `DeepEPTokenDispatcher.combine`, the scoring branch in `score_and_combine`, and the conditional `recompute`/pin there.

If DeepEP + gpt_oss/muse_spark must keep working, at least compute the "absorb?" bool once in `__init__` from the config, rather than with `isinstance` and `getattr` per forward.

Several docstrings and comments now describe the old behavior:
- the `combine_tokens` docstring still says the routing scores are applied here, says it takes "raw (unweighted)" outputs, and documents the removed `remat_region_name`/`recompute` args;
- `dispatch_tokens` (~489-506) says the scores are applied in `combine_tokens`, says `recompute` "must match" combine's (it no longer does), and gives a 3-tuple `Returns`;
- the module docstring (~33) and the effects comment (~113);
- the `DeepEPTokenDispatcher` class docstring (`token_dispatcher.py:828-832`: "A remat policy replays both").

The `_handle_cache` comment (~62) also deserves a line: under FullAC, "dispatch replayed, combine saved" is now the normal path, not an edge case.
